# Constitution

Hard stops for every task. Details: `.cursor/rules/playwright-conventions.mdc`.

## MUST

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Role-based locators | `getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId`. No CSS/XPath in new code. |
| Web-first assertions | `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` etc. Auto-wait; no manual sleeps. |
| `storageState` auth | Setup project + saved state. No UI login in every test. |
| Unique self-cleaning data | Unique names/ids; track + delete via API/`api-cleanup`. |
| One tag per test | Tag the `test(...)`, not the `describe`. |

## SHOULD

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Faker factories | Build test data via factories, not hand-rolled literals. |
| Enums for repeated strings | Shared labels, statuses, routes — one source of truth. |
| JSDoc on action methods | Document POM actions (params, side effects, returns). |

## WON'T

| Never | Why |
|-------|-----|
| XPath | Brittle; fails a11y-first locator policy. |
| `waitForTimeout` | Hides races; use web-first expects / event waits. |
| Hardcoded secrets | Env / CI secrets only. |
| `any` | Type the fixture, POM, and API shapes. |
| Weakened assertions | Don't delete, soften, or skip to go green. |
| Healing a real bug | Triage → `bug-reporter`. `self-heal` only for selector drift. |
| Tags on `describe` | Tag individual tests only. |

